                "jobTitle": "Group Deputy CEO and Premium, Midscale & Economy Division CEO",
                "lastName": "Morin",
                "photoUrl": "https://cdn-api.swapcard.com/public/images/96add8627cc94ae29086196e24ee65b6.jpeg",
                "organization": "Accor",
                "biography": "Jean-Jacques Morin is a graduate of the Ecole Nationale Supérieure de l'Aéronautique et de l'Espace, holds an MBA from Thunderbird School of Global Management (Arizona State University) and is qualified with the French Institute of Chartered Accountants, the Ordre des Experts Comptables.\n\nHe began his career with Deloitte where he spent five years in Audit and Consulting, first in Paris and then in Montreal. He continued to work internationally in the semiconductor sector for 13 years, at Motorola, ON Semi in Arizona, and lastly at Communicant AG, a Berlin-based start-up. He joined Alstom in 2005 as CFO for the Power sector in Zurich and then Transport sector, before being appointed Group CFO.\n\nJean-Jacques joined Accor’s Executive Committee as CFO in 2015 and was later appointed Deputy CEO responsible for Finance, Strategy, IT, Legal Affairs, Procurement and Communications.\n\nIn January 2023, in addition to his current role as Group Deputy CEO, he also took under his leadership the Group’s Premium, Midscale & Economy division as division CEO.",
