                "photoUrl": "https://cdn-api.swapcard.com/public/images/3e48bf508a3f4f5a855d9b179a19b4ec.jpeg",
                "organization": "UN Tourism",
                "biography": "Luis Nicolás Barrios Medina-Montoya, Innovation Education and Investments Regional\nManager for the UNWTO Regional Office in Riyadh.\nMaster in Project Management from Esden Business School. PMI-certified PMP. Master\nin Marketing and Commercial Management from IE Business School. Master in Audiovisual Production from IEEA. Degree in Audio-visual Communication from the University\nof Malaga.\nExpert in technology and innovation applied to the tourism sector. From February 2003\nuntil June 2020, he developed his professional career in Tourism in SEGITTUR, a stateowned company integrated into the Spanish Ministry of Industry Trade and Tourism and\nattached to the State Secretariat for Tourism, responsible for promoting innovation\n(R&D) in the Spanish tourism sector, both in the public sector.\nSince 2012 he was involved, in different capacities, in the development and\nmanagement of the Smart Tourist Destinations program. From 2019 to 2022 he was\nresponsible for the direction and coordination of all the Smart Tourism Destination\nProjects in Latin America, coordinating projects in Tequila, Medellín and Bogotá.\nIn 2018 he coordinated the Extremadura Smart Territory project, the first adaptation to\nan Autonomous Community of the Smart Tourism Destinations methodology.\nPreviously, he was responsible for the implementation of the technological\nmanagement tools of the Smart Tourist Destinations program, SEGITTUR’s mobile\napplication development projects, the deployment of the public WIFI network of El\nHierro (Canary Islands) and the design of the Volcanological Interpretation Centre of El\nHierro.\nCollaborating lecturer at IE Business School (since 2017). Collaborating lecturer at\nOstelea School of Tourism & Hospitality (since 2018).",
