                "organization": "Taiba Investments",
                "biography": "Muteb Jumaiah is a distinguished leader in Human Resources, currently serving as the Section Head of Organization Development at Taiba Investments in Riyadh. His expertise in strategic HR management has significantly enhanced organizational efficiency and culture.\n\nPrior to the merger, Muteb managed the merger transaction internally between Dur and Taiba Investment Co., overseeing the daily implementation of the project within an institutional framework. He was responsible for coordinating various components of the program and managing the entities involved, both internally and externally. His role also included managing risks and challenges and providing critical recommendations to the Steering Committee.\n\nFollowing the merger, Muteb has been instrumental in leading culture integration efforts, ensuring a seamless blend of corporate cultures and enhancing employee alignment with the new organizational goals. His strategic oversight continues to strengthen retention and competitiveness across the company.\n\nHolding a Bachelor’s Degree in Political Science and Government from St. Edward's University and a CIPD Level 5 Diploma in Human Resources Management, Muteb is further accredited as a KPI Professional, underscoring his expertise in performance management.\n\nMuteb's dynamic leadership and strategic perspective are fundamental in propelling the evolution of HR practices and instigating impactful industry-wide improvements.",
