                "jobTitle": "CEO",
                "lastName": "Callaert",
                "photoUrl": "https://cdn-api.swapcard.com/public/images/df060694a5bb4b8fa4b40f7907847040.jpeg",
                "organization": "Daniel Ost Group",
                "biography": "Yann Callaert is the CEO of Daniel Ost, one of the world's most prestigious flower houses, known for its exquisite designs and innovative approach to luxury floral events and retail. Yann blends his background in business management with his passions for luxury retail, events, art, and design.\n\nA graduate of Karel de Grote Antwerp University with a Bachelor's degree in International Business, Yann's early career was marked by numerous international internships and leadership as the captain of the university rugby team. His professional journey started at TrustedFamily, a high-profile consulting firm focused on family businesses. There, he was responsible for the strategic partnerships and he engaged with some of the world's most affluent families, further honing his expertise in business strategy and client relations.\n\nIn 2014, Yann joined Daniel Ost. Now as CEO, he has been instrumental in expanding the business while maintaining its commitment to creativity and quality. His strategic vision focuses on nurturing the brand's legacy alongside fostering innovation. Currently, Daniel Ost operates globally, with a local presence in Europe and the Middle East.\n\nBeyond his professional pursuits, Yann is deeply committed to community service and leadership. He is an active member and former leader within Round Table International and a founding board member of the Friendship Fund Foundation. In 2020, Yann was appointed as Honorary Consul for Ecuador in Belgium, where he supports Ecuadorian residents and facilitates international trade and diplomatic efforts.\n\nYann is also a strong advocate for lifelong learning, having completed Vlerick Business School's Executive Management Programme and the executive course on Managing a Luxury Brand at Christie's Education",
