                "organization": "Rua Al Madinah Holding Company",
                "biography": "Nadeem is the Chief Strategy Officer for Rua Al Madinah Holding (a wholly owned PIF company) where he is responsible for Group Strategy & Performance, EPMO and Operational Excellence. Prior to this he was Chief Advisor to the KSA Minister of Investment and instrumental in driving the National Investment Strategy underpinning Vision 203o.\n\nBefore joining the Ministry, Nadeem was the Advisor for Corporate Development and Transformation at Digital Dubai Authority where he managed Strategy, HR, Finance, Procurement, Legal, FM and HSE in addition to overseeing multiple group-wide and city level transformation and digitisation initiatives.\n\nPrior to Digital Dubai Nadeem was CEO of a private family office and has held many senior positions including Group Chief Strategy Officer for GEMS Education and before that various Vice President positions at Dubai World Trade Centre. Prior to moving to the Middle East in 2008 Nadeem was in Consulting and specialised in strategy delivery and business transformation for organisations such as Virgin and the insurance giant Prudential.\n\nNadeem holds a Global Executive MBA from TRIUM (partnership between London School of Economics (UK), Stern School of Business, New York University (USA) and HEC (France). He also holds a B.A (Hons) in Accounting & Financial Management from the University of Essex in the UK. He is a Fellow for both the Institute of Business Consulting and the Association for Project Management. He currently serves as a Board Member and Advisor for multiple companies in KSA and internationally.",
